    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting high-walk/high-speed matchups, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.25) and **Christian Yelich** (71.68). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top play; despite batting eighth, he faces a soft matchup against Fedde and benefits from a significant dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability environment for a stolen base\u2014a critical multiplier for our 5x5 constraints. **Christian Yelich** similarly benefits from the same favorable game environment against Ober, where his combination of a strong platoon split and favorable wind conditions secures his status as an elite start. Meanwhile, **Hyeseong Kim** (61.65) and **Carson Benge** (63.27) anchor the secondary tier, both boosted heavily by favorable SP xERA projections (17.18 and 6.75, respectively) that mitigate concerns regarding their lower lineup placement.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing the preservation of game caps over marginal starts. **Chase Meidroth** (49.85) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly failing to displace our infield core; while his base profile is respectable, his dynamic platoon penalty against the right-handed Rea ultimately pushed him below our internal efficiency thresholds. **Dillon Dingler** (39.99) landed just shy of our 40-point floor due to an aggressive platoon penalty, confirming his status as a bench asset today. Conversely, the high-upside bats of **Trea Turner** (48.87) and **Kyle Schwarber** (47.62) are active despite facing the elite arm of Skenes. While their raw scores are deflated by the pitching matchup, their inherent potential for explosive production\u2014and our need for category volume\u2014keeps them in the lineup, though owners should monitor the risk of suppressed batting averages against such a formidable opponent. We continue to hold **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** in reserve, awaiting more favorable entry points.",
